FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:426 — `run_code` seeds the analyzer with `session_names()`, which includes `"_"` from `self.variables` (inserted at src/repl/mod.rs:403), but the VM never binds `"_"` — `2 + 3` then `say _` passes the static check and fails at runtime with `Unknown variable '_'`, while `:vars`/`:inspect`/completion advertise `_` as readable — exclude `"_"` from the analyzer seed or bind the last result in the VM so static acceptance implies runtime resolution.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:295 — `exceeds_block_limits` is checked before `needs_continuation`, so a single complete line larger than `MAX_BLOCK_BYTES` (64KB) is dropped as an "incomplete block ... that never balanced" and never runs, though the same source runs via file — only enforce the line/byte cap while continuation is pending, or bypass it for input whose `open_block_depth` is already balanced.
3. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:659 — `replay` runs restored lines through `execute_line` with no end-of-replay `report_unclosed_block`, so a saved file ending in an unclosed block leaves `multiline_buffer`/`in_multiline` set and the next typed line is swallowed into a block the user never opened — drain/report the pending buffer after the loop as `run` does on EOF.
4. [MAJOR] src/repl/commands.rs:296 — `None => (spec.build)(None)` ignores any argument to a no-arg command despite the `CommandSpec` contract that `usage: None` "tells the parser it must not be given one", so `:quit foo`/`:vars bar`/`:reset baz` silently succeed with no test on that side — check `Self::argument(input)` on the `None` arm and report `Unknown`/`MissingArgument`-style usage instead of discarding it.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
